{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid","id":517348,"title":"After the monsters raid...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-17T14:41:02-07:00","id":517348,"title":"After the monsters raid...","content":"So my players in <b>Mage</b> game were captured by<i> Malleus Maleficarum</i> cell under the boarding school near the London. They killed main Inquisitor and his two more physical and one more technology inclined Hunters, but more social Hunters of cell were not harmed. So about half of hunters cell and 20 Malleus regular agents wait for sorceresses to come to their holy headquarters with the power of their Orders. Or should they?<br /> <br /> Questions are simple -<b> Should Hunters to stand the ground and defend their HQ? Or just pack everything and run, as being exposed? Or maybe they will pull strings in Vatican? What would your cells do in this situation? </b>Taking in to account you run an institution above your HQ and have two dozen of quasi-civilian agents under it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T15:27:29-07:00","id":517376,"title":"","content":"The first thing we would need to know before answering this is just how much damage the mages did, and how much did they take doing so?<br /> <br /> If the mages effortlessly fried/disintegrated/imploded their victims and got away without a scratch, that's going to trigger a different response in the hunters than if the mages got away only by the skin of their teeth and barely managed to kill anyone.<br /> <br /> That said, if it's the &quot;social geeks&quot; who survive, stripping down and relocating makes the most sense to me. These are the hunters who job in the Cell is to talk to people - they're not good at fighting by definition. Send an emergency dispatch to HQ for reinforcements, try to cover up their former locale (destroying evidence, etc), then clear out and regroup before sitting tight and waiting for reinforcements to arrive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T18:43:18-07:00","id":517503,"title":"","content":"For contacting the Vatican, that's gotta be a threshold for how bad things really are. If they did kill the local inquisitor (Who I'm presuming wasn't laity but an actual ordained member of the Church), that would go up the chain to a bishop or cardinal who would send a replacement, but if this is still local there might not be any major warnings to send to Rome just yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T00:47:12-07:00","id":517753,"title":"","content":"The first question I have, are your players powerful enough to get past the Blessed Protection Benediction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T04:31:12-07:00","id":517813,"title":"","content":"Blessed Protection is in the corebook or supplement? I used <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/499949-art-of-witch-hunting-htv-perspective?p=511117#post511117\">mine own Witch Hunters Endowments</a> for thing like Sympathy Dummy, or Ward against new spells. Still, Arrow PC get to understand how the Ward needs symbol to work.<br /> <br /> And the problem is not &quot;the PCs cabal is on the Malleus HQ trail&quot;. It's &quot;PCs want to call Guardians and Adamantine Arrow from whole London to take Witch Hunters out&quot;, rather thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T00:25:44-07:00","id":519041,"title":"","content":"What makes the best story for your group? After all, you control the NPCs. If the remaining hunters are rash, naive or fanatic enough they are going to stick around regardless of the power of the PCs. If they are cowards, cautious, and so on they are going to lay low, potentially placing various hidden camera's and lethal traps to deal with any intruders while observing their powers from a distance.<br /> <br /> As for assistance from other factions, the last time the players in my group asked their groups for help (in my case the Summer Court) it worked to some extend, but it would take time and the group decided that was not something they had.<br /> <br /> For my own group I would go for the cautious paranoid hunters (they tend to survive longer anyway). Abandon the HQ, but leave cameras and some very nasty traps. Of course, I would set a certain time required to set things up and see whether or not the PCs arrive on time to at least catch those people setting up the traps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T13:51:40-07:00","id":533598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=519041#post519041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes the best story for your group? After all, you control the NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking <b>Malleus</b> plot would make nice re-entry for our main plot of <b>Mage</b> game, but now it looks like as players will declare war on <i>Hammer of Witches</i>. I rather wanted to run a session, maybe two on this plot and return to main plot of chronicle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=519041#post519041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the remaining hunters are rash, naive or fanatic enough they are going to stick around regardless of the power of the PCs. If they are cowards, cautious, and so on they are going to lay low, potentially placing various hidden camera's and lethal traps to deal with any intruders while observing their powers from a distance.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Malleus</b> is defending thier <i><b>sacred</b></i> place where first christians in Britian gather. So they should be determined to defend the place. On the other hand, those hunters are martyrs, but not stupid. They understand &quot;witches&quot; can call the help. So the question is how to not escalate this to &quot;hunters are calling Vatican for back-up to kill all mages in London&quot; kinda scenario.<br /> <br /> When I think about it, maybe <b>Lord Stewards</b> should be used here? ( If someone do not know, <b>Lord Stewards</b> are fan conspiracy of Great Britain administration that is making pacts with monsters. They are in fanbook the <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/HtV/DreamCatchers.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a> ) Maybe social concerned Hammer on Witches would made Lords to talk with Orders and petition on non-violet solution to what Arrows and Guardians would need to sign in, to stop full on bloodshed?<br /> <br /> Also, other subtopic - <b><i>How</i> can Malleus hunt for witches from <u>centuries</u> and be not discovered to this times in region?</b> It looks like the Hunter corebooks assume that MM cells are sent from Vatican each time new case come, not that they operate in their region, like normal hunters. How can this be solved?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=519041#post519041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for assistance from other factions, the last time the players in my group asked their groups for help (in my case the Summer Court) it worked to some extend, but it would take time and the group decided that was not something they had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Players are not time pressed, as they know the Malleus will probably not send after them new forces, at least not from this HQ. They can take some days to gather connections from Orders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=519041#post519041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my own group I would go for the cautious paranoid hunters (they tend to survive longer anyway). Abandon the HQ, but leave cameras and some very nasty traps. Of course, I would set a certain time required to set things up and see whether or not the PCs arrive on time to at least catch those people setting up the traps.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is interesting idea and probably I will use it. Even then, maybe we could talk more about mine other sceanros above, or those &quot;death traps&quot; to be set in detail. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T05:18:57-07:00","id":535469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=533598#post533598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking <b>Malleus</b> plot would make nice re-entry for our main plot of <b>Mage</b> game, but now it looks like as players will declare war on <i>Hammer of Witches</i>. I rather wanted to run a session, maybe two on this plot and return to main plot of chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>than let hem kill off the hunters and remove any interesting traces leading to Vatican. <br /> <br /> <br /> But really, calling help from Vatican won't help against awakened if they play smart. Mages don't need to show up for a fight or call reinforcements. Now that they are informed where to look for inquisitors, hunters have lost the element of surprise. Depends on the players and you of course. For me a direct combat in Mage game is a last resort, several stronger spirits, hired gunman and 'gas leaks' could take care of nearly anybody. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T06:09:57-07:00","id":535501,"title":"","content":"If you want a quick fix you could have the MM be a puppet of the Paternoster Ministry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the question is how to not escalate this to &quot;hunters are calling Vatican for back-up to kill all mages in London&quot; kinda scenario. </div> </div> </div>Have you established that they have that capacity? London is not some backwater you can just send an army of hunters into. It'll be a logistical nightmare, where are they going to get their weapons from? How are they going to avoid the police and the security services when they start murdering people? Conversely, London is the consilium's own territory, they should be able to pull a lot of strings in their defence.<br /> <br /> You can handwave all that for sure, but there're plenty of plausible reasons for the Vatican to just cut their loses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, other subtopic - <b><i>How</i> can Malleus hunt for witches from <u>centuries</u> and be not discovered to this times in region?</b> It looks like the Hunter corebooks assume that MM cells are sent from Vatican each time new case come, not that they operate in their region, like normal hunters. How can this be solved? </div> </div> </div>Suspension of disbelief. Hunter is designed to have the players be members of the conspiracies, so you can hand wave how they keep secret.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T14:34:49-07:00","id":535945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=533598#post533598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, other subtopic - <b><i>How</i> can Malleus hunt for witches from <u>centuries</u> and be not discovered to this times in region?</b> It looks like the Hunter corebooks assume that MM cells are sent from Vatican each time new case come, not that they operate in their region, like normal hunters. How can this be solved?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but... discovered by WHO? Mages, or humans? It's really unclear from your post.<br /> <br /> If you're asking why the MM hasn't been discovered by the rest of humanity, that's easy: political deniability. The Vatican disavows any connection to these &quot;poor unfortunate souls&quot; who have gone crazy or who have succumbed to mortal sins or whatever, and people believe them. Even if the hunters aren't willing to take the fall for the good of the Church, nobody is going to believe that the Vatican, respected by millions of people as the true beacon of spiritual authority and moral law, God's voice on this earth, is secretly training anti-monster hitmen. People don't even believe in monsters, at least not openly; the cultural zeitgeist is such that anyone who admits to believing in monsters won't say so for fear of being persecuted as crazy.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you're asking how Mages haven't discovered them, who says they haven't? They don't destroy the MM because they can't use their powers that openly for something that elaborate; destroying the MM would at the least entail murdering dozens if not hundreds of priests in Vatican City and all over the world, destroying church-held libraries, and generally causing an uproar that wold echo across the world. And that's just to get rid of the current iteration; damaging the Vatican so they'd never get the idea of reviving the MM, at least not for some time, would be even more involved. To say nothing of the fact that the Seers probably offer their own covert support of the MM in the shadows, styming the efforts of the Orders should they deem that moving against some branch of the MM is called for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T22:58:46-07:00","id":536555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=535945#post535945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, if you're asking how Mages haven't discovered them, who says they haven't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't remember the exact book, but mages do know they exist, at least silver ladder and mystorium do. They don't target them because hunters don't target awakened mages 90+% of time and when they do it's probably someone that got it coming it somehow. SL has wast interests in Vatican and these hunters do kill the threats for humanity, doing more good than harm in the end. Plus the reasons you listed. <br /> <br /> Basically, any massive actions against hunters would be stimed by higher-ups. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T02:27:30-07:00","id":536761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=535501#post535501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a quick fix you could have the MM be a puppet of the Paternoster Ministry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was looking for some tie-ins to <b>Mage</b> in higher eschelons of MM that inspired this cell. Paternoster Obrimos giving &quot;encouragment&quot; is good scenario. Before, I was thinking about Gurardians of Veil in Vatican who forseen the PCs rise to Hieromagus, and they wanted to take them out as sensing next &quot;False Messiaha&quot; split. Will deside on what later on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=535501#post535501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you established that they have that capacity? London is not some backwater you can just send an army of hunters into. It'll be a logistical nightmare, where are they going to get their weapons from? How are they going to avoid the police and the security services when they start murdering people? Conversely, London is the consilium's own territory, they should be able to pull a lot of strings in their defence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also good point - so, basiclly, even members of Conspiracies like MM in <b>Hunter</b> are on they own, as the HQ would not them help if this would made &quot;supernatrual politics destability&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=535501#post535501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suspension of disbelief. Hunter is designed to have the players be members of the conspiracies, so you can hand wave how they keep secret.</div> </div> </div> </div>But MM should be active for centuries in London. It must be some deeper resolution to this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=535945#post535945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but... discovered by WHO? Mages, or humans? It's really unclear from your post.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was meaning mages, of course. And more - the local cells of Malleus Maleficarum that <b>should</b> hunt Awakened, from time to time. Those factions live in one city ( Orders and MM ), not in vacuum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=535945#post535945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, if you're asking how Mages haven't discovered them, who says they haven't? They don't destroy the MM because they can't use their powers that openly for something that elaborate; destroying the MM would at the least entail murdering dozens if not hundreds of priests in Vatican City and all over the world, destroying church-held libraries, and generally causing an uproar that wold echo across the world. And that's just to get rid of the current iteration; damaging the Vatican so they'd never get the idea of reviving the MM, at least not for some time, would be even more involved. To say nothing of the fact that the Seers probably offer their own covert support of the MM in the shadows, styming the efforts of the Orders should they deem that moving against some branch of the MM is called for.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make here good points. So Consillium shuld be aware of Hunters organizations in local vicnity and talk to Awakened as &quot;do not make to much noice and do not break Precept of Secrecy or we will have unnecessary diplomatic precedent with them&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=536555#post536555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, any massive actions against hunters would be stimed by higher-ups.</div> </div> </div> </div>On <b>both</b> sides - Vatican would not want open war from Italy, Orders know that Hunters can rally Sleepers that outnamber any mage groups in region. Typical politcal stalemate.<br /> <br /> So, in the end, stiaution looks like that Hunters can hunt on the wizards outsie of protection from Orders - and Orders will &quot;throw a bone&quot; of some really degenerated Awakened for Hunters, so they should not start open Witch Hunting? Is this typical setting situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T03:15:26-07:00","id":536770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But MM should be active for centuries in London. It must be some deeper resolution to this... </div> </div> </div>Why not just have them operate from the Vatican? Do you really need them to work as a local cell?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so, basiclly, even members of Conspiracies like MM in <b>Hunter</b> are on they own, as the HQ would not them help if this would made &quot;supernatrual politics destability&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Not really. My point was that you're assuming the MM have the resources to fight the London consilium. That doesn't have to be true if it's going to mess your story up. Maybe the MM only have one cell in London, maybe they can't easily replace that cell. That's a reasonable possibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Orders know that Hunters can rally Sleepers that outnamber any mage groups in region. </div> </div> </div>How exactly? And what's stopping magi (or your players) doing exactly the same thing? If your priest starts talking about murdering random people for being witches, that's not very convincing. Further, the MM still have to use weapons, so they're already breaking some pretty serious laws. All the consilium needs to do is point the police in the direction of the MM and they've got themselves an army of sleepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T03:39:52-07:00","id":536776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=536770#post536770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not just have them operate from the Vatican? Do you really need them to work as a local cell?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have ancient Christian burial site that were made an MM local base - at least - 200 years ago. And it's this place the PCs mages braught to and they escaped.<br /> <br /> Also, from the reading of <b>Hunter</b> books I get idea that Conspiracies have local chapter as much as in every European country...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=536770#post536770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. My point was that you're assuming the MM have the resources to fight the London consilium. That doesn't have to be true if it's going to mess your story up. Maybe the MM only have one cell in London, maybe they can't easily replace that cell. That's a reasonable possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Little reasonable as <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglicanism#Ordinariates_within_the_Roman_Catholic_Church\" target=\"_blank\">Anglicans now can easily become Catholics</a>. In that term, I though MM would be on rise in England.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T04:17:59-07:00","id":536793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, from the reading of <b>Hunter</b> books I get idea that Conspiracies have local chapter as much as in every European country... </div> </div> </div>So? Change it. They're a one-off antagonist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Little reasonable as <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglicanism#Ordinariates_within_the_Roman_Catholic_Church\" target=\"_blank\">Anglicans now can easily become Catholics</a>. In that term, I though MM would be on rise in England. </div> </div> </div>Not if it's going to make youir game harder to run. Becoming Catholic doesn't mean you automatically sign up for membership in an unofficial paramilitary deathsquad. The MM are a very small group when you consider they have a potential pool of hundreds of millions of people to recruit from. Baudolino has kept his grasp on the organisation by keeping the leadership pretty restricted to the people he can personally recruit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T05:08:14-07:00","id":536813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=536776#post536776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They have ancient Christian burial site that were made an MM local base - at least - 200 years ago. And it's this place the PCs mages braught to and they escaped.<br /> <br /> Also, from the reading of <b>Hunter</b> books I get idea that Conspiracies have local chapter as much as in every European country...<br /> <br /> <br /> Little reasonable as <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglicanism#Ordinariates_within_the_Roman_Catholic_Church\" target=\"_blank\">Anglicans now can easily become Catholics</a>. In that term, I though MM would be on rise in England.</div> </div> </div> </div>No matter how you look at it the hunters are helpless in the current situation. Look on it from the other side. Mages would be basically slaughtering helpless non-combatants for what amounts to revenge. Play up on that. Would the players have the stomach to kill terrified and helpless people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T06:44:53-07:00","id":536941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=536793#post536793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So? Change it. They're a one-off antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly - I used them to show that World of Darkness is deeper than Pentacle vs Seers conflict, from <b>Mage</b> perspective. Maybe, later, I would want to return to Malleus Maleficarum subplot ( or throw them as recurring backup antagonists ), just I do not want players to concentrate on them to make it full on war.<br /> <br /> I think that &quot;your higher-ups, after talk with Lords Stewards, do not agree to open action&quot;. Only thing is this - players want to go for Adaminitne Arrow and Guardians of Veil for help - both Orders should help in this situation ( well, GotV maybe more in reason to cut the thing now, so to better preaper next move ).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/517348-after-the-monsters-raid?p=536793#post536793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not if it's going to make youir game harder to run. Becoming Catholic doesn't mean you automatically sign up for membership in an unofficial paramilitary deathsquad. The MM are a very small group when you consider they have a potential pool of hundreds of millions of people to recruit from. Baudolino has kept his grasp on the organisation by keeping the leadership pretty restricted to the people he can personally recruit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. But I will have a more Catholics in rise of the Islands as other excuse, to threaten the Consillium. Mages do not know everything. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T14:43:25-07:00","id":537435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Good point. But I will have a more Catholics in rise of the Islands as other excuse, to threaten the Consillium. Mages do not know everything. </div> </div> </div>Wow. That's sounds pretty hilarious.<br /> On a side note the offer to allow Anglican groups to join the Catholic church is less the reason for an increase in Catholic population than recent migration within the EU from comparatively new member states such as Poland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}